WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.200
Small businesses everywhere ask the same big question: are we sustainable?

2
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:09.600
But no single standard can say yes.

3
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:16.200
Standards come and go, differ by region and industry, and buyers keep changing what they ask.

4
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:20.600
Without an expert on staff, most small businesses can’t keep up.

5
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:25.450
MOSAIC is a sustainability navigator for small and medium enterprises.

6
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.390
It distills many standards into one knowledge base,

7
00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:34.770
then focuses on what matters to your location, industry, size, markets, buyers and goals.

8
00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.920
Take one question: do you have a written environmental policy?

9
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:43.470
It appears in eleven of forty-four source documents, twenty-three times in all.

10
00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:49.200
Recurrence between documents counts seventy-five percent; within documents, twenty-five.

11
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:53.460
That sets its base weight: three point eight six out of five.

12
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.290
Your context can raise it, never lower it.

13
00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:02.750
So you get clear scores, practical recommendations, and Levers to test what-if changes,

14
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:10.600
each grounded in real documents and aligned with your goals, so you know where to focus first.

15
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:15.150
And buyers get better supplier data, because you have the right records ready

16
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:20.600
when a questionnaire or procurement audit arrives.

17
00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:22.960
Sustainability…

18
00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.000
Sustainability always depends.

19
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.250
MOSAIC.

20
00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.800
The pieces that matter.
